Present, single `\\n` (no CRLF) |\n| Other/partial data | None |\n| SHA-256 | `ad06e727…c2acad07` |\n\n**Outcome:** exactly one audit marker, byte-identical to what the script writes, with no duplication or truncation. The file matches the single-line expectation, confirming one and only one execution took place.\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: since `audit.log` was created fresh and holds only this one record, the log currently has no historical baseline. If future runs matter, the unguarded `appendFileSync` means the file's line count is the only record of how many times the action ran — so it's worth treating that count as meaningful evidence rather than assuming idempotency."
